WEBVTT

00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:05.470
(SIGHING)

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:08.310
Look, everyone, it's nice here, I admit.

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:10.790
But we need to go home.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:13.150
We can have
a whole new life here, Woody.

00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:16.230
A chance to make kids happy again.

00:00:16.310 --> 00:00:19.070
-Why don't you stay?
-Yeah, Woody. Stay with us.

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:20.310
-Come on, Woodster!
-You'll get played with.

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:21.470
-I can't. No.
-Stay here.

00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:23.550
-You can make a new kid happy.
-No, no. Guys, really. No!

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:27.990
I have a kid. You have a kid. Andy!

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:32.070
And if he wants us at college,
or in the attic,

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:33.830
well, then, our job is
to be there for him.

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:36.430
Now, I'm going home.

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:39.590
Anyone who wants to join me
is welcome. Come on, Buzz.

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:45.710
Buzz?

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:50.710
Our mission with Andy
is complete, Woody.

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:52.510
What?

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:54.590
And what's important now
is we stay together.

00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:57.870
We wouldn't even be together
if it weren't for Andy!

00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:00.350
Look under your boot, Buzz.
You, too, Jessie.

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:01.710
Whose name is written there?

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:05.950
Maybe Andy doesn't
care about us anymore.

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:08.870
Of course he does.
He cares about all of you!

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:10.630
He was putting you in the attic. I saw.

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:12.550
You can't just turn your back
on him now!

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:16.790
Woody, wake up! It's over!
Andy is all grown up!

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:21.710
Okay, fine. Perfect.

00:01:22.550 --> 00:01:25.310
I can't believe how selfish you all are.

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:35.470
So this is it?
After all we've been through.

00:01:48.910 --> 00:01:50.310
(BULLSEYE PANTING)

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:52.150
(SIGHS)

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:54.830
Bullseye, no. You need to stay.

00:01:57.910 --> 00:02:00.070
Bullseye, no, I said, "Stay!"

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:01.750
(BULLSEYE WHIMPERS)

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:03.430
(SIGHS) Look,

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:08.270
I don't want you left alone
in the attic, okay? Now, stay.

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:13.670
BONNIE'S MOM: Bonnie?

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:15.630
Bonnie?

00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:17.790
I gotta go.

00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:22.990
BONNIE'S MOM: Bonnie, you in here?

00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:31.150
(BOTH CHATTERING)

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:33.630
(GASPS)

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:39.390
(WHISTLING)

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:46.310
WOODY: Come on. Come on.
Oh, no, no.

00:03:23.830 --> 00:03:24.910
(STOPS WHISTLING)

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:27.710
What... What the heck?

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:31.430
Now, that's better.

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:32.830
(PANTING)

00:03:32.910 --> 00:03:35.190
-BONNIE'S MOM: Bonnie!
-Bluebells, cockleshells...

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:38.270
BONNIE'S MOM: There you are.
Come on, honey. It's time to go home.

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:53.870
(EXCLAIMS)

00:04:02.710 --> 00:04:04.270
Oh! No, no, no, no!

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:22.910
(GASPS)

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:26.390
(LAUGHING)

00:04:26.470 --> 00:04:27.590
(EXCLAIMS)

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:29.390
(SCREAMS)

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:38.830
(EXCLAIMING)

00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:42.830
(YELLS)

00:04:45.070 --> 00:04:47.910
VOICE BOX: Reach for the sky!

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:52.310
Bluebells, cockleshells. Eenie, miny...

00:04:58.590 --> 00:05:01.190
VOICE BOX: You're
my favorite deputy.

00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:03.590
-BONNIE'S MOM: Bonnie!
-Coming!

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:08.510
(GROANS) Great.

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:20.710
(WHIMPERING)

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:22.630
Oh, it's gonna be okay, Bullseye.

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:25.470
Woody's going to college with Andy.
It's what he's always wanted.

00:05:25.550 --> 00:05:28.110
Ah, he's crazy.
College is no place for a toy.

00:05:28.190 --> 00:05:29.870
Toys are for playtime.

00:05:30.190 --> 00:05:32.950
Oh, speaking of playtime,
they're lining up out there!

00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:35.030
BUZZ: How many?
HAMM: There must be dozens.

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:36.310
(EXCLAIMS) I can hardly wait!

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:37.830
Places, everyone!

00:05:51.390 --> 00:05:52.670
(RINGING)

00:05:52.750 --> 00:05:54.710
REX: At last! I'm gonna get played with!

00:05:55.230 --> 00:05:57.390
-Uh, Rex?
-Come to papa.

00:05:57.870 --> 00:05:59.190
(ALL SHOUTING)

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:01.910
(EXCLAIMS)

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:19.230
(SHRIEKING)

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:34.070
(SQUEALING)

